{"raw": {"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/60152": {"title": "Adjunct - Clinical Instructor", "description": "Adjunct - Clinical Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/151551": {"title": "Adjunct Professor Biochemistry", "description": "Adjunct Professor Biochemistry You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/212651": {"title": "Assistant Director of Admission-School of Nursing", "description": "Assistant Director of Admission-School of Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221392": {"title": "Assistant Director of Development", "description": "Assistant Director of Development You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/222968": {"title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid", "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/196314": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing", "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/214918": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Practice", "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/218668": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Public Health (tenure track)", "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Public Health (tenure track) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221714": {"title": "Benefits Manager", "description": "Benefits Manager You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Benefits Manager McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $65,000.00 - $80,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Job Shift Any Category Human Resources Apply Description Office of Human Resources FLSA Status: Exempt Reports To: Director of Human Resources FTE: 1.0 Department: Human Resources Effective Date: October 2026 Join Our Team Linfield University is seeking an experienced and knowledgeable Benefits Manager to serve as the university\u2019s subject matter expert and primary owner of employee benefit programs. This is an excellent opportunity for a benefits professional who enjoys combining employee service, data analysis, compliance, vendor management, and strategic program improvement in a collaborative university environment. Job Summary The Benefits Manager serves as the university\u2019s subject matter expert and primary owner of employee benefit programs. This position independently manages the administration, compliance, analysis, and continuous improvement of employee benefits and retirement programs. The Benefits Manager partners with employees, Human Resources, Payroll, Finance, brokers, carriers, retirement vendors, and third-party administrators to ensure accurate administration, strong employee service, regulatory compliance, data integrity, and effective benefit strategy. Essential Job Duties Provides functional ownership and subject matter expertise for the university\u2019s employee benefit programs, including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term and long-term disability, flexible spending and health spending accounts, and the 403(b) retirement plan. Leads annual benefit renewal and open enrollment processes, including plan evaluation, system configuration and testing, employee communications, enrollment support, carrier coordination, and post-enrollment reconciliation. Partners with insurance brokers and benefit vendors to evaluate plan performance, utilization, cost trends, market competitiveness, vendor performance, and opportunities for plan design improvements. Analyzes benefit utilization, enrollment, cost, benchmarking, and financial data and develops recommendations regarding benefit strategy, plan design, employee contributions, and cost management. Owns benefit data integrity and reconciliation processes across HRIS, payroll, carriers, retirement vendors, and other benefit systems, identifying discrepancies and ensuring accurate employee deductions and employer contributions. Conducts regular benefit audits and reconciliations, researches discrepancies, determines root causes, and coordinates timely corrections with internal teams and external vendors. Maintains benefit administration processes and records in accordance with applicable requirements, including ERISA, HIPAA, COBRA, ACA, FMLA, PLO, OFLA, and other applicable federal and Oregon requirements. Provides retirement plan administration support and serves as a key resource for the university\u2019s 403(b) plan, including eligibility, enrollment, contribution administration, vendor coordination, reconciliation, employee education, and compliance support. Participates in retirement plan committee meetings and supports required plan governance, audits, reporting, documentation, and follow-up activities. Serves as the primary HR liaison with benefit carriers, brokers, retirement vendors, and third-party administrators, monitors service levels, resolves escalated issues, and holds partners accountable for timely and accurate service. Provides employees with clear information and assistance regarding benefit eligibility, enrollment, qualifying life events, plan provisions, claims questions, and available resources. Supports employees with leave-related information and directs employees to the university\u2019s third-party leave administrator for leave intake, documentation, eligibility, certification, and administration. Coordinates benefit-related information with the third-party administrator and internal stakeholders as needed. Partners with Payroll and Finance to ensure accurate benefit deductions, employer contributions, invoicing, funding, and financial reconciliation. Develops and maintains employee benefit communications, educational materials, procedures, and resources that are accurate, understandable, and accessible. Plans and coordinates benefit education events, benefit fairs, wellness initiatives, and other employee benefit programming as appropriate. Maintains current knowledge of employee benefit legislation, regulatory guidance, industry trends, and best practices and recommends process or plan changes when appropriate. Develops, documents, and improves benefit procedures, internal controls, workflows, and service standards to support consistent and efficient administration. Provides guidance and benefit expertise to Human Resources colleagues and university leaders and collaborates on cross-functional initiatives involving benefit programs, systems, and employee experience. Provides professional, responsive, and confidential service to faculty, staff, managers, supervisors, and university leadership. Performs other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Finance, or a related field and a minimum of five years of progressively responsible employee benefits experience. An equivalent combination of education and directly related benefits experience may be considered in lieu of a degree. Demonstrated expertise administering complex employee benefit programs, including health and welfare benefits and retirement plans. Demonstrated knowledge of ERISA, HIPAA, COBRA, ACA, FMLA, PLO, and other applicable federal and state benefit requirements. Demonstrated experience with benefit reconciliation, data auditing, annual enrollment, vendor management, and employee benefit communications. Experience working with HRIS, payroll, benefit administration, or carrier systems and the ability to identify and resolve data discrepancies across systems. Experience working directly with brokers, carriers, retirement plan vendors, and third-party administrators. Strong analytical skills and demonstrated ability to interpret benefit, financial, utilization, and benchmarking data and translate findings into practical recommendations. Demonstrated ability to independently research complex benefit issues, exercise sound judgment, evaluate alternatives, and recommend solutions. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to explain complex benefit information clearly to employees and leaders. Excellent organizational, research, problem-solving, and project management skills, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Demonstrated ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with professionalism and discretion. Preferred Qualifications Professional certification such as CEBS, PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, or SHRM-SCP. Experience administering a 403(b) retirement plan. Experience in higher education or another complex, multi-population organization. Experience with Oracle. Experience with benefit system implementation, configuration, testing, or data conversion. Physical Requirements Work is primarily performed in an office environment and involves regular use of a computer and other standard office equipment. The position requires the ability to communicate effectively, remain stationary for periods of time, move throughout campus as needed, and occasionally lift or carry materials weighing up to 20 pounds. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Apply Today If you are an experienced benefits professional who values accuracy, employee service, collaboration, and continuous improvement, we encourage you to apply and bring your expertise to Linfield University\u2019s Human Resources team. Linfield University participates in E-Verify to verify the identity and work eligibility of all new employees. To apply, please submit your application materials through the Linfield University employment portal. We look forward to learning more about how your experience and passion align with our mission. https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221714 Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221960": {"title": "Boiler Plant and Fleet Services Specialist", "description": "Boiler Plant and Fleet Services Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/58494": {"title": "Bus Driver", "description": "Bus Driver You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Bus Driver McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $34.00 Apply Description Position Type: Part time / Temporary position Job Summary: As an Athletics Bus Driver, you'll play a crucial role in providing safe and reliable transportation for our athletics teams. Reporting to the Bus Manager and/or Athletic Director, you'll ensure the smooth operation of our bus services, maintaining accurate records, and upholding exemplary customer service standards. Your responsibilities include safe driving practices, reporting any issues promptly, and maintaining cleanliness standards for the bus. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Operate University-owned buses and vehicles as assigned, ensuring compliance with all relevant policies and regulations. Maintain a valid Commercial Driver's License (CDL), Class B minimum, with a passenger endorsement. Adhere to Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration and Oregon Law requirements. Maintain records of duty status and comply with driving limitations set forth by regulations. Uphold Linfield University's Sexual Harassment and Discrimination policies under Title IX. Submit necessary paperwork promptly, including reimbursement requests and receipts. Ensure the safety and comfort of passengers during transportation. Qualifications: Minimum 21 years of age. Proficient in English for effective communication and record-keeping. Experience and training in safe motor vehicle operation. Possess a valid medical examiner's certificate. Clean driving record with no more than one valid motor vehicle violation in the past 3 years. Familiarity with driving regulations and safety protocols. Ability to adhere to driving limitations and maintain accurate records. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements: Duties performed on a school bus, subject to various environmental factors including noise, fumes, and weather conditions. Physical ability to perform emergency evacuation procedures, including pushing/pulling up to 50 pounds. Comfortable with frequent sitting, reaching, bending, and kneeling. Excellent vision abilities including close, distance, night, color, and peripheral vision. Work Environment: The work environment may involve loud noise levels and exposure to various elements. Reasonable accommodations can be made for individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Join our team and contribute to the success of our athletics program by ensuring safe and efficient transportation for our teams! Apply now and become an integral part of Linfield University Athletics. Linfield University participates in E-Verify to verify the identity and work eligibility of all new employees. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/220695": {"title": "Director of Annual Giving", "description": "Director of Annual Giving You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/213012": {"title": "Director of Marketing", "description": "Director of Marketing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221982": {"title": "HVAC, Ventilation and Fleet Services Technician", "description": "HVAC, Ventilation and Fleet Services Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/60183": {"title": "Linfield Public Safety Officer I", "description": "Linfield Public Safety Officer I You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Linfield Public Safety Officer I McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Apply Description Job Title: Campus Public Safety Officer Job Summary: Join our team at Linfield University as a Campus Public Safety Officer, where you'll play a crucial role in providing safety and security services to our campus community. You'll be responsible for various duties including emergency response, patrolling campus grounds, enforcing university policies, and ensuring a safe environment for all. If you're passionate about keeping others safe and thrive in dynamic environments, we want you on our team. Work Schedule: Flexible schedule with occasional shift rotations to accommodate varying assignments. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Patrol campus premises via vehicle, foot, or bicycle to deter crime and enforce parking policies. Engage with individuals on campus to ensure they have legitimate reasons for being on university property. Conduct regular checks of buildings and grounds to maintain safety and security. Respond to calls for service, incidents, accidents, and potential crimes. Document incidents and conduct follow-up investigations as needed. Assist with crowd control and traffic management during university events. Collaborate with other campus departments and emergency services to provide support and assistance. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED with at least one year of safety/security experience or equivalent training. Strong interpersonal and problem-solving skills. Clear and effective communication abilities, both oral and written. Ability to remain composed and diffuse tense situations. Quick and objective decision-making skills. Familiarity with investigative procedures and documentation. Proficiency in computer operations. Oregon DPSST certification as an unarmed private security professional (or obtainable within 90 days). First Aid/CPR/AED certification (or obtainable within 90 days). Valid Oregon driver's license with a good driving record. Physical Requirements: Ability to perform physically demanding tasks in various weather conditions. Capable of constant observation, communication, and physical exertion. Comfortable with lifting up to 100 pounds, operating vehicles, and being at risk for bodily harm in the line of duty. If you're ready to make a difference in campus safety and security, apply now to join our dedicated team of professionals at Linfield University. Linfield University is committed to fostering a community where all students, staff, and faculty feel a strong sense of inclusion and belonging. We believe that a vibrant, inclusive environment strengthens academic excellence and critical thinking. We welcome applicants with varied identities, backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences, and encourage candidates to share how their professional and personal experiences, teaching, scholarship, mentorship, or service will contribute to our efforts. Linfield University participates in E-Verify to verify the identity and work eligibility of all new employees. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/58615": {"title": "Linfield Public Safety Officer I On-Call", "description": "Linfield Public Safety Officer I On-Call You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Linfield Public Safety Officer I On-Call McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Apply Description Provide safety and security services to the Linfield University community in a variety of situations including emergency response. Follow established security policies and standard operating procedures as outlined by the Director of Linfield Public Safety. Enforce university policies and appropriate state laws on the campus property by monitoring and patrolling the grounds and buildings of the university. Perform standard crime, fire/life safety, and accident prevention duties including investigation and documentation of incidents. Maintain and provide for the university a log and other documentation of activities while at work in this capacity. Work Schedule: Depends on assignment; Flexibility is required to accommodate occasional shift rotations as needed. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Patrol the campus in either a security vehicle, on foot, or bicycle to provide a safe and secure environment by deterring crime and enforcing university parking policy. Contact people on the university property who are not members of the Linfield community and ensure they are either guests or have appropriate business on the campus. Ensure the safety and security of campus facilities by making frequent checks of buildings and grounds. Ensure that buildings are locked and secured after certain hours for protection of persons and property. Respond to calls for service and reports of incidents, accidents, and/or possible crimes Observe and report suspicious and/or criminal activity. Take appropriate action as the situation requires: Use presence and verbal commands to mitigate suspicious activity on campus. Complete incident/investigation reports. Conduct follow-up investigation and interview persons in connection with the investigation. Secure evidence pertaining to the incident. Respond to emergency situations and summon emergency medical assistance and/or apply first aid, interview principles and witnesses . Make general drawings of the accident scene and complete accident forms. Perform crowd control duties and traffic management duties for university events. Document and, when possible, correct fire/life safety hazards. Work closely and cooperatively with other members and departments of the Linfield community. Respond to medical emergencies, render initial aid, and summon emergency medical assistance . Cooperate with and work closely to provide support service to both the Police and Fire Departments when they respond to the campus. Linfield Public Safety personnel are considered \"essential employee positions\" with the university and are subject to work during emergency incidents and closing of the university or its campuses, in addition to institutional holidays and break periods. A complete loss of communication (phone, internet, etc.) is to be considered a campus emergency. If a regional or large-scale event occurs in which an officer would reasonably believe that their assistance may be needed on campus, the officer should attempt to contact the department. If they cannot reach the department, they should respond to the campus. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED, and at least one year of safety/security experience or equivalent educational training. Experience must demonstrate: Excellent interpersonal skills and problem resolution skills. Ability to clearly and precisely communicate both orally and in writing. Ability to maintain composure in stressful situations, control a situation, and diffuse anger or hostility in others. Able to analyze a situation quickly and objectively to determine the correct course of action. Knowledge of written documentation procedures and tampering of evidence and standard investigative procedures. Ability to work effectively with a varied campus community. Computer skills necessary for operating systems, producing reports, etc. Possess Oregon DPSST certification as an unarmed private security professional or obtain professional certification within 90 days of date of hire. Possess First Aid/CPR/AED certification or obtain certification within 90 days of date of hire. Possess valid Oregon driver's license, have a good driving record, and ability to become and remain certified as a driver of university vehicles. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work is classified as heavy work of a physical nature in a campus environment with exposure to weather elements working indoors and outdoors. Work involves constant observation, verbal communication, walking, bicycling, running, climbing stairs, and standing; frequent stooping, kneeling, crouching, pushing, pulling and lifting up to 100 pounds, and operating a motor vehicle. Incumbent is at risk for bodily harm or injury in the course of the job. Linfield University is committed to fostering a community where all students, staff, and faculty feel a strong sense of inclusion and belonging. We believe that a vibrant, inclusive environment strengthens academic excellence and critical thinking. We welcome applicants with varied identities, backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences, and encourage candidates to share how their professional and personal experiences, teaching, scholarship, mentorship, or service will contribute to our efforts. Linfield University participates in E-Verify to verify the identity and work eligibility of all new employees. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221385": {"title": "Pre-K Substitute Teacher", "description": "Pre-K Substitute Teacher You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pre-K Substitute Teacher McMinnville Campus - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.55 Hourly Position Type Full-Time or Part-Time Apply Description Substitute Teacher \u2013 Linfield Pre-Kindergarten Linfield Pre-Kindergarten is seeking enthusiastic, dependable substitute teachers to join our team on an on-call, as-needed basis. This is a great opportunity for individuals who enjoy working with young children in a supportive, child-centered, and family-friendly learning environment. Job Description Linfield Pre-Kindergarten is recruiting for substitute teachers. The Pre-K provides 2.5-hour pre-k sessions two days a week for children who are 3-4 years of age, and 2.5-hour pre-k sessions three days a week for children who are 4-5 years of age. In addition, the pre-k serves as a training program for Linfield University education students gaining direct experience working with children in a classroom environment in conjunction with their coursework. The Pre-K is a child-centered, family friendly program that supports developmentally appropriate practices. Job summary: Substitute teachers are responsible for providing instruction to preschoolers and managing the classroom environment in the absence of the regular teacher. The position is an on-call, as-needed position that can be short or long-term depending on need of the regular teacher. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Implement and teach lesson plans and instructions as directed by the absent teacher and consult with the director or assistant director for further directions Work with intern and work-study staff to set up the classroom for the day\u2019s activities, manage the daily schedule and clean-up materials/equipment Implement developmentally appropriate practices maintaining an environment that is respectful to all and providing positive guidance and discipline to the children Supervise children at all times and maintain a safe environment Keep records on accidents, injuries, and incidents Communicate in a friendly and positive manner towards families, preschoolers and staff Leaves notes for the regular teacher at the end of the teaching day Qualifications: Child Development Associate (CDA) credential and at least one year experience in an early childhood program, or an equivalent combination of experience and education demonstrating knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties of the job Registered in the Central Background Registry through the Office of Child Care Knowledge and experience with developmentally appropriate practices Understanding of effective positive classroom management practices and principles Effective communication, interpersonal and teamwork skills Recognizing child abuse and neglect training CPR and First Aid certification Preferred Qualifications: Food handlers permit Yearly medical training administrating medications If you are passionate about supporting young children and would enjoy contributing to a welcoming early-learning environment at Linfield University, we encourage you to apply. Linfield University participates in E-Verify to verify the identity and work eligibility of all new employees. To apply, please submit your application materials through the Linfield University employment portal. We look forward to learning more about how your experience and passion align with our mission. https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221385 Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/209477": {"title": "Simulation Operations Specialist II", "description": "Simulation Operations Specialist II You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/210362": {"title": "Systems Manager - Slate Enrollment Management", "description": "Systems Manager - Slate Enrollment Management You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Systems Manager - Slate Enrollment Management Fully Remote \u00a0 \u2022 \u00a0 Remote Location - McMinnville, OR 97128 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,000.00 - $70,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's Degree Travel Percentage None Category Admissions Apply Description Systems Manager \u2013 Slate Enrollment Management Location: Remote Department: Admissions Employment Type: Full-time, Exempt Join Linfield University At Linfield University, you\u2019ll be part of a collaborative, mission-driven community dedicated to student success. Our Enrollment Management team plays a vital role in helping prospective students discover a transformative educational experience. We are seeking an innovative, data-driven Systems Manager to lead the administration and strategic use of our Slate CRM while partnering across campus to enhance the student recruitment and enrollment experience. If you enjoy optimizing systems, improving business processes, and using technology to drive meaningful results, we\u2019d love to hear from you. Position Summary The Systems Manager serves as the division\u2019s lead expert for the Slate CRM, providing strategic leadership, technical expertise, and operational support for Enrollment Management. As the University\u2019s primary Slate administrator (\u201cSlate Captain\u201d), this position oversees system configuration, data integrity, workflow optimization, reporting, and integrations that support undergraduate recruitment and admissions operations. Working closely with Undergraduate Admission, Graduate Admission, Financial Aid, Information Technology Services, and other campus partners, the Systems Manager develops innovative solutions that improve efficiency, enhance the user experience, and support institutional enrollment goals. What You\u2019ll Do Lead Slate CRM Strategy & Administration Serve as the University\u2019s functional lead and primary administrator for the undergraduate Slate CRM. Configure and maintain workflows, automations, applications, forms, portals, events, communications, and system functionality. Ensure Slate supports recruitment strategies, operational excellence, and enrollment objectives. Evaluate new features and implement enhancements that improve performance and user experience. Manage Data, Reporting & Analytics Develop and maintain queries, dashboards, and reports that support strategic planning and operational decision-making. Provide regular and ad hoc reporting to admissions leadership and campus stakeholders. Maintain the integrity, accuracy, and consistency of prospective student data. Analyze trends and support enrollment forecasting and data-informed planning. Support Admissions Operations Optimize admissions processes including application management, review workflows, scholarship programming, and decision release. Support efficient processing of a high-volume applicant pool. Partner with admissions staff to improve daily operations and eliminate process barriers throughout the enrollment lifecycle. Improve Business Processes Continuously evaluate and streamline workflows across the admissions lifecycle. Establish operational standards, documentation, and best practices that promote consistency and scalability. Lead CRM-related initiatives that strengthen enrollment operations and support institutional goals. Collaborate with campus partners and participate on cross-functional committees to advance strategic priorities. Collaborate on Systems Integration Work with Information Technology Services, TechSolutions, and campus partners to develop, test, and maintain integrations between Slate, Ellucian Colleague, and other third-party systems. Test new functionality while ensuring data security, reliability, and system integrity. Serve as the primary liaison for CRM enhancements, upgrades, and issue resolution. Train & Support Users Create and maintain user guides, workflow documentation, and operating procedures. Deliver training and ongoing support for admissions and campus users. Promote best practices that expand institutional knowledge and effective use of Slate. Continue Professional Growth Stay current with emerging trends and best practices in CRM administration, enrollment technology, and admissions operations. Participate in professional development opportunities and implement innovative solutions that improve enrollment outcomes. What You\u2019ll Bring Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Five or more years of professional experience demonstrating expertise in CRM systems, data management, business processes, and project management. Minimum two years of advanced experience administering Slate CRM, including complex query development (such as configurable joins). Experience with database structures and CRM-to-ERP integrations, preferably Ellucian Colleague or comparable systems. Demonstrated success improving business processes and implementing operational efficiencies. Proven ability to manage complex, cross-functional projects involving multiple stakeholders. Strong analytical, investigative, and problem-solving skills with a continuous improvement mindset. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Experience leading, mentoring, or supervising professional staff. Preferred Knowledge & Skills Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Strong customer service orientation and collaborative working style. Sound judgment, discretion, and ability to maintain confidentiality. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and welcoming environment for individuals from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Ability to communicate the value of a liberal arts education and support the mission of Linfield University. Work Schedule This remote position typically works Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. PST. Flexibility is required to support occasional evening and weekend activities related to student recruitment and enrollment. Why Join Linfield University? At Linfield, you\u2019ll join a close-knit community where innovation, collaboration, and student success are at the heart of everything we do. Your work will directly support the University\u2019s enrollment strategy by improving systems, streamlining processes, and helping prospective students navigate their path to becoming members of the Linfield community. If you\u2019re passionate about leveraging technology, data, and process improvement to make a meaningful impact, we encourage you to apply. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | \u00a9 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/221993": {"title": "Utilities Maintenance Technician", "description": "Utilities Maintenance Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app."}}, "rows": {"https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/60152": {"school_id": 1113, "posting_url": "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/F16D49EDEBF447BF71AEBC32D5AF6AB5/jobs/60152", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct - Clinical Instructor", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Clinical Instructor", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal